# TODO - Specification and legacy-interpreter execution modes

## Objective

Make specification-conformant execution the only normal Malbolge semantics while
retaining an explicit `legacy-ben` mode for archaeology, differential diagnosis,
and historical-corpus study.

## Acceptance

- Normal execution follows the normative target specification and never enables
  historical interpreter defects implicitly.
- `legacy-ben` is explicit, safe to disable completely, and cannot satisfy
  normal compiler/verifier conformance obligations.
- Observable state, I/O, termination, diagnostics, and mode identity are covered
  by positive and discrepancy fixtures.
- The declared scope contains no unresolved placeholder implementation or
  undocumented workaround required for this objective to function.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.

## Evidence

- Expected durable artifact surface: `vm/`, `execution/`, `tests/vm/`,
  `benchmarks/interpreter/`.
- Required evidence: specification fixtures, explicit legacy discrepancy
  fixtures, and differential traces against independent implementations; Ben
  interpreter comparison is limited to its documented agreement domain.
- Current implementation evidence is
  `src/runtime/virtual-machine/domain/mode.rs`,
  `src/runtime/virtual-machine/domain/execution.rs`,
  mode-aware tracing in `src/runtime/virtual-machine/domain/machine.rs`, and
  `tests/vm/modes.rs`.
- Default builds reject `legacy-ben`; feature-enabled tests cover H-001 and
  H-002 behavior while H-003 and H-004 remain explicit safe failures. Mode
  identity is asserted in traces and diagnostics, and verifier eligibility is
  normative-only.
- Implementation evidence is present. Completion remains gated on the declared
  repository-wide `jig validate --root .` command passing at retirement time.
- Prerequisite completion evidence: `safe-rust-malbolge-vm`,
  `historical-undefined-behavior-catalogue`.
